{"name":"Sambuca","hex":"#3b2e25","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sambuca","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Italian liqueur made from elderberries and flavoured with licorice, traditionally served with 3 coffee beans that represent health, wealth and fortune (or past, present and future)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An ancient form of triangular harp having a very sharp, shrill tone.","An ancient type of ship-borne siege engine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sambuca"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sambuca","blocks":[{"text":"Sambuca is an Italian anise-flavoured liqueur. Its most common variety is often referred to as \"white sambuca\" to differentiate it from other varieties that are deep blue or bright red. Like other anise-flavoured liqueurs, the ouzo effect is sometimes observed when combined with water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Sambuca_1l.jpg/330px-Sambuca_1l.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sambuca","wikidata":"Q723464"},{"title":"Sambuca (instrument)","blocks":[{"text":"The sambuca was an ancient stringed instrument of Asiatic origin. The term sambuca is also applied to a number of other instruments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Fresco_of_women_listening_to_a_private_musical_performance.jpg/330px-Fresco_of_women_listening_to_a_private_musical_performance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sambuca_(instrument)","wikidata":"Q827200"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/A_reconsturction_of_a_sambuca%2C_Kotsanas_Musuem_of_Ancient_Greek_Technology.jpg/500px-A_reconsturction_of_a_sambuca%2C_Kotsanas_Musuem_of_Ancient_Greek_Technology.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia